module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Stalk
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Fiber
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.Sheaf
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Stalk
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.AssociatedPrime.Basic
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Stalks of scheme-theoretic fibres, associated points and the relative assassin

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of schemes, `y : Y`, and `p` a point of the scheme-theoretic
fibre `f.fiber y` with image `x = f.fiberι y p` in `X`. This file identifies the local ring of
the fibre at `p` with the quotient of `𝒪_{X,x}` by the ideal generated by the image of the
maximal ideal of `𝒪_{Y,y}`:
`𝒪_{X_y, p} = 𝒪_{X,x} / 𝔪_y·𝒪_{X,x}`.

This is the identification the Stacks Project uses without comment when it writes
`B/𝔪_A B = 𝒪_{X_s, x}` in the proof of More on Morphisms, Lemma 0GSI, and it is the bridge
that turns a statement about the fibres of a morphism into a statement of commutative algebra
about a stalk. The file also fixes the vocabulary of that lemma: the associated points of a
sheaf of modules (Tag 02OJ) and the relative assassin `Ass_{X/S}(ℱ)` (Tag 05AT).

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal f x`: the ideal `𝔪_{f x}·𝒪_{X,x}` of `𝒪_{X,x}`
  generated by the image of the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{Y,f x}` under the stalk map of `f`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.fibreStalk f x` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.toFibreStalk f x`: the quotient `𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_{f x}·𝒪_{X,x}` and
  the projection onto it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsAssociatedPoint` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.associatedPoints`: Tag 02OJ, parts (1) and (2) — a point is
  associated to an `𝒪_X`-module when the maximal ideal of the local ring there is an associated
  prime of the stalk.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeAssassin`: Tag 05AT, the relative assassin.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.ker_stalkMap_fiberι`: the kernel of the stalk map of
  `f.fiberι y` at `p` is exactly `stalkFibreIdeal f (f.fiberι y p)`. Together with the
  surjectivity of that stalk map — `f.fiberι y` is a preimmersion — this is the identification
  above, packaged as `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.fibreStalkRingEquiv` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.fibreStalkIso`, and pinned down by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.toFibreStalk_fibreStalkIso_hom`: the isomorphism carries the
  projection to the stalk map, so it really is *the* canonical comparison and not merely an
  abstract isomorphism of the two rings.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.bijective_stalkMap_fiberι`: when the maximal ideal of
  `𝒪_{Y,f x}` generates the zero ideal in `𝒪_{X,x}` — for instance at a point lying over the
  generic point of an integral `Y`, where that maximal ideal is already zero, by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal_eq_bot` — the fibre has the same local ring as
  `X`. This is the step that identifies `(N ⊗_A K)_𝔮` with the stalk of `ℱ_t` at `y` in 0GSI.

## Implementation notes

Nothing is narrowed: every result is stated for an arbitrary morphism of `Scheme.{u}` with `u`
a universe variable, as Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.fiber` forces, and the point of
the fibre is an arbitrary point rather than one of the canonical points `f.asFiber x`.

The theorem is stated as an equality of the *kernel* of the stalk map with
`stalkFibreIdeal`, rather than directly as an isomorphism, because that form is what the
consumers need (an element of the stalk dies in the fibre exactly when it lies in
`𝔪_y·𝒪_{X,x}`) and because it makes the canonicality clause above a `rfl`.

The source point is spelled `f.fiberι y p` throughout and the base point as `f (f.fiberι y p)`
rather than `y`, even though the two agree. This is not cosmetic: `(f.fiberι y ≫ f) p` and
`f (f.fiberι y p)` are definitionally but not syntactically equal, and keeping one spelling is
what lets the comparison isomorphisms be stated without transport.

`stalkFibreIdeal` is the ideal generated by the image of `𝔪_{f x}`, i.e. `Ideal.map`, and not
the comap of anything; it is the ideal written `𝔪_A B` in the Stacks Project.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GSI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GSI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05AT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AT)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits IsLocalRing TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)

/-- The ideal of `𝒪_{X,x}` generated by the image of the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{Y,f x}`. -/
noncomputable def Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal (x : X) : Ideal (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
  Ideal.map (f.stalkMap x).hom (maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (f x)))

/-- A local homomorphism of local rings carries the maximal ideal into the maximal ideal. -/
private theorem map_mem_maximalIdeal {R S : CommRingCat.{u}} [IsLocalRing R] [IsLocalRing S]
    (φ : R ⟶ S) [IsLocalHom φ.hom] {a : R} (ha : a ∈ maximalIdeal R) :
    φ.hom a ∈ maximalIdeal S := by
  rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff]
  exact fun h ↦ (IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal a).mp ha (isUnit_of_map_unit _ a h)

/-- The stalk map of `f` is a local homomorphism, so `𝔪_{f x}·𝒪_{X,x}` is a proper ideal. -/
theorem Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal_le_maximalIdeal (x : X) :
    f.stalkFibreIdeal x ≤ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
  exact fun a ha ↦ map_mem_maximalIdeal (f.stalkMap x) ha

/-- `𝔪_{f x}·𝒪_{X,x}` is not the unit ideal. -/
theorem Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal_ne_top (x : X) : f.stalkFibreIdeal x ≠ ⊤ :=
  fun h ↦ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal (X.presheaf.stalk x)).ne_top
    (top_le_iff.mp (h ▸ f.stalkFibreIdeal_le_maximalIdeal x))

/-- The closed fibre of a stalk is a nonzero ring. -/
instance Scheme.Hom.nontrivial_quotient_stalkFibreIdeal (x : X) :
    Nontrivial ((X.presheaf.stalk x) ⧸ f.stalkFibreIdeal x) :=
  Ideal.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr (f.stalkFibreIdeal_ne_top x)

/-- The quotient `𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_{f x}𝒪_{X,x}`. -/
noncomputable def Scheme.Hom.fibreStalk (x : X) : CommRingCat.{u} :=
  CommRingCat.of ((X.presheaf.stalk x) ⧸ f.stalkFibreIdeal x)

/-- The projection `𝒪_{X,x} ⟶ 𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_{f x}𝒪_{X,x}`. -/
noncomputable def Scheme.Hom.toFibreStalk (x : X) : X.presheaf.stalk x ⟶ f.fibreStalk x :=
  CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (f.stalkFibreIdeal x))

/-- The ring `𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_{f x}𝒪_{X,x}` is nonzero. -/
instance (x : X) : Nontrivial (f.fibreStalk x) :=
  f.nontrivial_quotient_stalkFibreIdeal x

/-- The ring `𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_{f x}𝒪_{X,x}` is local. -/
instance (x : X) : IsLocalRing (f.fibreStalk x) :=
  IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (Ideal.Quotient.mk (f.stalkFibreIdeal x))
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

/-- The projection `𝒪_{X,x} ⟶ 𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_{f x}𝒪_{X,x}` is a local homomorphism. -/
instance (x : X) : IsLocalHom (f.toFibreStalk x).hom :=
  IsLocalHom.of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mk (f.stalkFibreIdeal x))
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

/-- The stalk of `Spec κ(y)` at the image of a point of the fibre has trivial maximal ideal,
because it is isomorphic to the field `κ(y)`. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_stalk_fiberToSpecResidueField_eq_bot (y : Y) (p : f.fiber y) :
    maximalIdeal ((Spec (Y.residueField y)).presheaf.stalk
      (f.fiberToSpecResidueField y p)) = ⊥ := by
  rw [← IsLocalRing.isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq]
  refine ((Spec (Y.residueField y)).presheaf.stalkCongr
    (Inseparable.of_eq (f.fiberToSpecResidueField_apply y p))).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.isField ?_
  exact (stalkClosedPointIso (Y.residueField y)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.isField
    (Field.toIsField _)

/-- The image of `𝔪_y` dies in the local ring of the fibre, because the fibre is a scheme over
`Spec κ(y)`. This is the easy half of `ker_stalkMap_fiberι`. -/
theorem Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal_le_ker_stalkMap_fiberι (y : Y) (p : f.fiber y) :
    f.stalkFibreIdeal (f.fiberι y p) ≤ RingHom.ker ((f.fiberι y).stalkMap p).hom := by
  have hpt : f (f.fiberι y p)
      = Y.fromSpecResidueField y (f.fiberToSpecResidueField y p) := by
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, f.fiber_fac y, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply]
  have e1 : (f.fiberι y ≫ f).stalkMap p
      = f.stalkMap (f.fiberι y p) ≫ (f.fiberι y).stalkMap p :=
    Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp _ _ _
  have e2 := Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_congr_hom (f.fiberι y ≫ f)
    (f.fiberToSpecResidueField y ≫ Y.fromSpecResidueField y) (f.fiber_fac y) p
  have e3 := Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp (f.fiberToSpecResidueField y)
    (Y.fromSpecResidueField y) p
  have e4 : f.stalkMap (f.fiberι y p) ≫ (f.fiberι y).stalkMap p
      = (Y.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq hpt)).hom
        ≫ ((Y.fromSpecResidueField y).stalkMap (f.fiberToSpecResidueField y p)
          ≫ (f.fiberToSpecResidueField y).stalkMap p) := by
    rw [← e1, e2, e3]
    try rfl
  rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
  intro a ha
  have h1 := map_mem_maximalIdeal
    ((Y.fromSpecResidueField y).stalkMap (f.fiberToSpecResidueField y p))
    (map_mem_maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq hpt)).hom ha)
  rw [maximalIdeal_stalk_fiberToSpecResidueField_eq_bot, Ideal.mem_bot] at h1
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker]
  refine (DFunLike.congr_fun (CommRingCat.hom_ext_iff.mp e4) a).trans ?_
  show ((f.fiberToSpecResidueField y).stalkMap p).hom
      (((Y.fromSpecResidueField y).stalkMap (f.fiberToSpecResidueField y p)).hom
        ((Y.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq hpt)).hom.hom a)) = 0
  rw [h1, map_zero]

/-- If a morphism `Spec R ⟶ Z` out of the spectrum of a local ring lies over
`Spec.map q ≫ X.fromSpecStalk (ι p)` along `ι` and hits the point `p`, then the kernel of the
stalk map of `ι` at `p` is contained in the kernel of `q`. -/
private theorem ker_stalkMap_le_ker_of_lift
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (ι : Z ⟶ X) (p : Z) {R : CommRingCat.{u}} [IsLocalRing R]
    (q : X.presheaf.stalk (ι p) ⟶ R) [IsLocalHom q.hom] (w : Spec R ⟶ Z)
    (hw : w ≫ ι = Spec.map q ≫ X.fromSpecStalk (ι p))
    (hpw : w (closedPoint R) = p) :
    RingHom.ker (ι.stalkMap p).hom ≤ RingHom.ker q.hom := by
  subst hpw
  have h1 : SpecToEquivOfLocalRing X R (w ≫ ι)
      = ⟨ι (w (closedPoint R)), q, inferInstance⟩ := (Equiv.eq_symm_apply _).mp hw
  obtain ⟨h2, h3⟩ := SpecToEquivOfLocalRing_eq_iff.mp h1
  have h4 : ι.stalkMap (w (closedPoint R)) ≫ Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo w
      = (X.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq h2)).hom ≫ q :=
    (Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo_comp w ι).symm.trans h3
  have hid : (X.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq h2)).hom = 𝟙 _ :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes_refl _ _
  intro a ha
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker] at ha ⊢
  have h5 := DFunLike.congr_fun (CommRingCat.hom_ext_iff.mp h4) a
  have h6 : (Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo w).hom
      ((ι.stalkMap (w (closedPoint R))).hom a) = 0 := by rw [ha, map_zero]
  have h7 : q.hom ((X.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq h2)).hom.hom a) = 0 :=
    h5.symm.trans h6
  have h8 : (X.presheaf.stalkCongr (Inseparable.of_eq h2)).hom.hom a = a :=
    DFunLike.congr_fun (CommRingCat.hom_ext_iff.mp hid) a
  exact h8 ▸ h7

private theorem fromSpecStalk_comp_apply_closedPoint {R : CommRingCat.{u}} [IsLocalRing R]
    (x : X) (φ : X.presheaf.stalk x ⟶ R) [IsLocalHom φ.hom] :
    (Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x) (closedPoint R) = x :=
  (Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ _).trans
    ((congrArg (fun z ↦ X.fromSpecStalk x z) (Spec_closedPoint (f := φ))).trans
      Scheme.fromSpecStalk_closedPoint)

/-- **The stalk of a scheme-theoretic fibre.** For a point `p` of `f.fiber y` with image
`x = f.fiberι y p`, the stalk map `𝒪_{X,x} ⟶ 𝒪_{X_y,p}` has kernel exactly the ideal generated
by the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{Y,y}`. Since that stalk map is surjective (`f.fiberι y` is a
preimmersion), this says `𝒪_{X_y,p} = 𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_y·𝒪_{X,x}`. -/
theorem Scheme.Hom.ker_stalkMap_fiberι (y : Y) (p : f.fiber y) :
    RingHom.ker ((f.fiberι y).stalkMap p).hom = f.stalkFibreIdeal (f.fiberι y p) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (f.stalkFibreIdeal_le_ker_stalkMap_fiberι y p)
  rw [← show RingHom.ker (f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p)).hom = f.stalkFibreIdeal (f.fiberι y p)
    from Ideal.mk_ker]
  have hfx : f (f.fiberι y p) = y :=
    (f.range_fiberι y ▸ Set.mem_range_self p : f.fiberι y p ∈ f ⁻¹' {y})
  have hker : ∀ a ∈ maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (f (f.fiberι y p))),
      (f.stalkMap (f.fiberι y p) ≫ f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p)).hom a = 0 :=
    fun a ha ↦ Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)
  set ψ₀ : Y.residueField (f (f.fiberι y p)) ⟶ f.fibreStalk (f.fiberι y p) :=
    CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.lift _
      (f.stalkMap (f.fiberι y p) ≫ f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p)).hom hker) with hψ₀
  have hres : Y.residue (f (f.fiberι y p)) ≫ ψ₀
      = f.stalkMap (f.fiberι y p) ≫ f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p) := by
    ext a; rfl
  have hfr : Y.fromSpecResidueField (f (f.fiberι y p))
      = Spec.map (Y.residue (f (f.fiberι y p)))
        ≫ Y.fromSpecStalk (f (f.fiberι y p)) := rfl
  have hsq : (Spec.map (f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p)) ≫ X.fromSpecStalk (f.fiberι y p)) ≫ f
      = Spec.map ((Y.residueFieldCongr hfx).inv ≫ ψ₀) ≫ Y.fromSpecResidueField y := by
    rw [Spec.map_comp, Scheme.residueFieldCongr_inv]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
    rw [Scheme.residueFieldCongr_fromSpecResidueField, hfr, ← Spec.map_comp_assoc, hres,
      Spec.map_comp_assoc, Scheme.SpecMap_stalkMap_fromSpecStalk]
  have hu := fromSpecStalk_comp_apply_closedPoint (f.fiberι y p)
    (f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p))
  have key : Limits.pullback.lift _ _ hsq ≫ f.fiberι y
      = Spec.map (f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p)) ≫ X.fromSpecStalk (f.fiberι y p) :=
    Limits.pullback.lift_fst _ _ hsq
  refine ker_stalkMap_le_ker_of_lift (f.fiberι y) p (f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p))
    (Limits.pullback.lift _ _ hsq) key ?_
  exact (f.fiberι y).isEmbedding.injective
    ((Scheme.Hom.comp_apply _ _ _).symm.trans
      ((congrArg (fun m : Spec (f.fibreStalk (f.fiberι y p)) ⟶ X ↦
        m (closedPoint (f.fibreStalk (f.fiberι y p)))) key).trans hu))

/-- The canonical ring isomorphism `𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_{f x}𝒪_{X,x} ≅ 𝒪_{X_{f x}, p}` for a point `p`
of the scheme-theoretic fibre with image `x`. -/
noncomputable def Scheme.Hom.fibreStalkRingEquiv (y : Y) (p : f.fiber y) :
    f.fibreStalk (f.fiberι y p) ≃+* (f.fiber y).presheaf.stalk p :=
  (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (f.ker_stalkMap_fiberι y p).symm).trans
    (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective
      ((f.fiberι y).stalkMap_surjective p))

/-- The comparison isomorphism carries the projection to the stalk map of the fibre
inclusion. -/
@[simp]
theorem Scheme.Hom.fibreStalkRingEquiv_toFibreStalk (y : Y) (p : f.fiber y)
    (a : X.presheaf.stalk (f.fiberι y p)) :
    f.fibreStalkRingEquiv y p ((f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p)).hom a)
      = ((f.fiberι y).stalkMap p).hom a := rfl

/-- The scheme-theoretic fibre has stalk `𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_{f x}𝒪_{X,x}`. -/
noncomputable def Scheme.Hom.fibreStalkIso (y : Y) (p : f.fiber y) :
    f.fibreStalk (f.fiberι y p) ≅ (f.fiber y).presheaf.stalk p :=
  (f.fibreStalkRingEquiv y p).toCommRingCatIso

/-- The comparison isomorphism is the canonical one: it carries the projection
`𝒪_{X,x} ⟶ 𝒪_{X,x}/𝔪_y·𝒪_{X,x}` to the stalk map of the fibre inclusion. -/
theorem Scheme.Hom.toFibreStalk_fibreStalkIso_hom (y : Y) (p : f.fiber y) :
    f.toFibreStalk (f.fiberι y p) ≫ (f.fibreStalkIso y p).hom
      = (f.fiberι y).stalkMap p := rfl

/-- Over a point whose local ring is a field — for instance the generic point of an integral
scheme — the fibre ideal is zero. -/
theorem Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal_eq_bot (x : X)
    (h : maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (f x)) = ⊥) : f.stalkFibreIdeal x = ⊥ := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkFibreIdeal, h, Ideal.map_bot]

/-- Where the fibre ideal vanishes the fibre has the same local ring as the source. -/
theorem Scheme.Hom.bijective_stalkMap_fiberι (y : Y) (p : f.fiber y)
    (h : f.stalkFibreIdeal (f.fiberι y p) = ⊥) :
    Function.Bijective ((f.fiberι y).stalkMap p) :=
  ⟨(RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mpr ((f.ker_stalkMap_fiberι y p).trans h),
    (f.fiberι y).stalkMap_surjective p⟩

/-- A point `x` of `X` is an associated point of an `𝒪_X`-module `F` when the maximal ideal of
`𝒪_{X,x}` is an associated prime of the stalk `F_x`. -/
noncomputable abbrev Scheme.Modules.IsAssociatedPoint {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (F : X.Modules) (x : X) : Prop :=
  let M : _root_.PresheafOfModules.{u}
    (X.presheaf ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}) := F.val
  letI : Module (X.presheaf.stalk x)
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) M.presheaf x) := inferInstance
  maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ∈
    associatedPrimes (X.presheaf.stalk x)
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) M.presheaf x)

/-- The set of associated points of an `𝒪_X`-module.

This and `Scheme.Modules.IsAssociatedPoint` above are the `AddCommGrpCat`-stalk encoding of
**Stacks 02OJ** parts (1) and (2). The tag is registered on
`Stacks.Divisors.IsAssociatedPoint`, `Stacks.Divisors.associatedPoints` and
`Stacks.Divisors.schemeAssociatedPoints`, which carry all three parts of the tag; these two are
kept because the relative-assassin development below is stated in this encoding. -/
noncomputable abbrev Scheme.Modules.associatedPoints {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (F : X.Modules) : Set X :=
  {x | Scheme.Modules.IsAssociatedPoint F x}

/-- The relative assassin `Ass_{X/S}(F)` of an `𝒪_X`-module over a morphism `f : X ⟶ S`: the
union over the points of `S` of the images in `X` of the associated points of the restriction of
`F` to the scheme-theoretic fibre. -/
noncomputable def Scheme.Hom.relativeAssassin {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)
    (F : X.Modules) : Set X :=
  ⋃ s : S, f.fiberι s ''
    Scheme.Modules.associatedPoints ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (f.fiberι s)).obj F)

/-- A point lies in the relative assassin exactly when it is the image of an associated point of
the restriction of the module to one of the scheme-theoretic fibres. -/
theorem Scheme.Hom.mem_relativeAssassin_iff {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) (F : X.Modules)
    (x : X) :
    x ∈ f.relativeAssassin F ↔
      ∃ (s : S) (xs : f.fiber s),
        Scheme.Modules.IsAssociatedPoint ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (f.fiberι s)).obj F) xs ∧
          f.fiberι s xs = x := by
  simp only [Scheme.Hom.relativeAssassin, Set.mem_iUnion, Set.mem_image,
    Scheme.Modules.associatedPoints, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]

end AlgebraicGeometry
